<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SOURCE OF TRUTH KEYWORDS: NSMicrophoneUsageDescription, LSUIElement,
    Info.plist, TCC, accessory
  WHAT:  macOS bundle keys Tauri merges into the generated Info.plist.
  WHY:   NSPersonalVoiceUsageDescription is the same kind of key for Voice mode:
         asking macOS to let the app speak in the user's Personal Voice without it
         is refused (and on some versions kills the process), so the prompt text is
         declared here.
         NSMicrophoneUsageDescription is NOT optional. Without it the app does
         not get DENIED microphone access — the process is killed by the OS on
         first access, which presents as a crash with no message.
         LSUIElement keeps Vocs out of the Dock and the app switcher, which
         is what makes it a background utility rather than a window you manage.
  WHERE: Merged at bundle time; read by the OS, never by our code.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Vocs needs your microphone to turn what you say into text. Audio is transcribed on this Mac and is never uploaded.</string>
    <key>NSPersonalVoiceUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Vocs can speak what you dictate in your own Personal Voice, for example into a meeting. Nothing leaves this Mac.</string>
    <key>LSUIElement</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
